d know that Kepler's Laws are a direct consequence of Newton's Law of Universal Gravitation together with his laws of motion.","sz":24.5,"c":"#3D3D3D","f":"Patrick Hand"}]}]},{"t":"text","box":[3.958,73.333,9.792,5.741],"anchor":"m","p":[{"al":"c","lh":0.854,"r":[{"x":"ES.4.7","sz":19.0,"b":1,"c":"#3D3D3D","f":"Cabin Sketch"}]}]},{"t":"text","box":[15.104,72.778,77.844,21.111],"anchor":"t","p":[{"al":"l","lh":0.827,"r":[{"x":"Create diagrams or models to demonstrate the effect of the gravitational pull of the sun and moon on Earth's oceans. Explain the difference between daily (high and low) tides and monthly (spring and neap) tides. Explain how monthly tides relate to the revolution of the moon, and therefore its phases.","sz":24.5,"c":"#3D3D3D","f":"Patrick Hand"}]}]}],"bg":"paper-fb1cb725.webp"}]}